# PantryPool Licensing Model

PantryPool is distributed under a dual-licensing / source-available model:

1. **Community Edition (Source-Available Core)**:
   The core PantryPool application and single-tenant communal breakroom platform are licensed under the **Functional Source License, Version 1.1, MIT Future License (FSL-1.1-MIT)** below. You are free to view, modify, and self-host the community edition for internal household, office, or organization use without software fees. However, offering PantryPool as a competing hosted or managed cloud service is prohibited until the rolling 2-year Change Date, after which each release converts automatically to the MIT License.

2. **Managed SaaS Cloud Fleet & Enterprise Modules**:
   Certain enterprise-grade modules (multi-tenant fleet orchestration, automated SAML/OIDC SSO, and managed cloud billing pipelines) are proprietary to the PantryPool SaaS platform.

